// If First is used then "history" is in descending order: 5, 4, 3, 2, 1. So look ahead for the
// "previousSiteConfig". If Last is used then "history" is in ascending order: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. So
// look behind for the "previousSiteConfig".
//
// In either case the item at the boundary of the slice has a nil "previousSiteConfig" and that
// is okay, because we will truncate it from the end result being returned. The user did not
// request this. _We_ fetched an extra item to determine the "previousSiteConfig" of all the
// items.
if paginationArgs.Last != nil {
